 * the managing agent line is Swiss Cottage's), who applies for the trade
 * permit (a search snippet only).
 *
 * WHOSE WORDS. From what he approved: the wardrobe guide's lines on
 * traditional panelled doors ("A cornice, suitable handles and carefully
 * chosen panel proportions can connect the wardrobe with existing woodwork.
 * The details should suit the scale of the room rather than compete with
 * it.") and on storage around the bed; the alcove guide's lines on
 * traditional alcove units, on the scale of mouldings, on combining the two
 * styles, and on the balance of base cupboards and shelving (the first FAQ,
 * said there of alcove units); the guarantee as worded on the other area
 * pages (Hampstead's fuller approved form says "structural integrity" and
 * "return and adjust"); the fitted wardrobe and alcove price lines as
 * approved on Hampstead. One conduct line: parking, deliveries and access
