 * (People also ask, over bed storage cupboards: "How to add storage above
 * bed?", made a whole question); UK, English, desktop, 17 Nov 2026.
 * The other questions in those boxes were costs, "cheaper" or "cheapest"
 * (the area rules item 10), retailers, or do-it-yourself. Answers from what
 * he approved: the alcove guide's layout and style sections, and the
 * wardrobe guide's storage around the bed.
 *
 * CHECKED 17 Nov by three independent reviewers (copy rules, facts against
 * the facts file and approved text, the swap test against the nine other
 * area pages). Changed on their findings: the first FAQ answer no longer
 * repeats Primrose Hill's alcove answer; the opening lost a "from X to Y"
 * sweep and West Hampstead's "as well as its room" shape; the description
 * is under 155 characters; the crescent drawing now has three floors over a
 * basement, as the Formosa Street text beside it says; the listed count
 * says what the leaflet says (it includes houses, villas and flats around
 * the four streets); listed and Grade II are explained at first use; the
 * Planning Portal sentence is no longer West Hampstead's; the certificate
 * line is Westminster's own; the trade permit's zone is the source's words;
 * each section's product paragraph opens on a local hinge (a mid-19th
 * century villa, the moulded window detail, a mansion-flat bedroom); the
 * third FAQ answers its question first; the leaflet and overview are named;
 * the stucco gloss, the third meta and the prices heading differ from the
 * other pages. Kept: his guide lines word for word, hedges included, as on
 * the other area pages, with two bracketed glosses (cornice, plinths) added
 * after a re-check; the three FAQ answers stay on his approved wording (area
 * rules item 10), so they carry no local fact on purpose. The re-check also
 * named Historic England in the Formosa Street line, put the bed recess in
